      "comment": "Classically <span lang=\"la\">rotātus</span> is the participle of <span lang=\"la\">rotāre</span>, “whirl round” (Ov., Quint.), so the phrase says “a board spun round”, not “a board on wheels”; Vitruvius’s <span lang=\"la\">subrotātus</span> is the word for wheeled. Andresian has <span lang=\"la\">tabulā rotātā vehī</span>, “ride a skateboard”."
    }
